%I A398454 #30 Oct 10 2026 15:06:59
%S A398454 1,1,1,1,1,57,1,10,1,1960,1,328085644,1,203,1512,3,1,1025524890,1,9,7,
%T A398454 181984,1,3247257600,1,11520,3,1069735,1
%N A398454 a(n) = (A383505(n)+1)/n.
%C A398454 Every solution k of binomial(k*n, k+1) == -1 (mod n) satisfies k == -1 (mod n), by the absorption identity (k+1)*binomial(k*n, k+1) = k*n*binomial(k*n-1, k). Hence A383505(n)+1 is divisible by n and a(n) is an integer. If there is no solution, then a(n) = 0.
%C A398454 a(n) = 1 (that is, A383505(n) = n-1) for n = 1 and for every n in A000430 (primes and squares of primes). Among n <= 1000, a(n) = 1 also for n = 125 and n = 343 and for no other n.
%C A398454 a(30) > 3.3 * 10^11.
%F A398454 a(A000430(n)) = 1.
%e A398454 a(6) = 57 because A383505(6) = 341 = 6*57 - 1.
%e A398454 a(12) = 328085644 because A383505(12) = 3937027727 = 12*328085644 - 1.
%Y A398454 Cf. A383505, A000430.
%K A398454 nonn,more,new
%O A398454 1,6
